    "title": "Preston Community Calendar | Preston County News | wvnews.com",
    "text": "Sunday, May 17\nThe McGrew Society will feature its collection of McGrew-Hagans’ family artifacts at the McGrew House in Kingwood during a special event at 1 p.m. Some artifacts have come directly from descendants of Persis Hagans McGrew. Others have come from community members who recognized the McGrew name. The program will start in Mr. McGrew’s library. Guests will also receive a newly printed “Walking Tour Guide” to follow as they explore other rooms such as the Antique Clothing Room, Dr. Kotchek’s Veterinary Museum, and the McGrew Homestead Room. The program is free to the public and will end with light refreshments.",
    "summary": "The McGrew Society will feature its collection of McGrew-Hagans’ family artifacts at the McGrew House in Kingwood during a special event at 1 p.m. Some artifacts have come directly from descendants of Persis Hagans McGrew. Others have come from community members who recognized the McGrew name. Guests will also receive a newly printed “Walking Tour Guide” to follow as they explore other rooms such as the Antique Clothing Room, Dr. Kotchek’s Veterinary Museum, and the McGrew Homestead Room. The program is free to the public and will end with light refreshments.",
